{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Step-7 sweep/parity census for avoided-flannel-eeve.\n\nInvariant: a stale ticket-store write-lock mkdir artifact must not block a mutating operation once the waiter has obtained the authoritative same-tracker kernel fcntl leg; holder diagnostics must not label an unqualified pid-number match as a proven live owner.\n\nConstruct sweep: `rg \"kill\\([^,]+,\\s*0\\)|pid_alive|ProcessLookupError\" src/rebar` found only `rebar._store.lock_owner._pid_alive` as the process-liveness probe used by lock ownership. `rg \"_mkdir_lock_is_stale|stamped_file_is_stale|_stamp_is_stale|_describe_stamped_pid\" src/rebar` found one staleness authority (`lock_owner._stamp_is_stale`) reached by the mkdir write lock and stamped-file locks; no duplicate staleness implementation needs a second fix.\n\nChannel census:\n- CLI command: mutating CLI paths go through `event_append` / `txn._acquire_write_lock` / `lock.write_lock`, so the shared `lock_owner` fix applies.\n- MCP/API tool: `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py` `log_session` -> `rebar.append_session_log` -> shared append/write lock; new `tests/interfaces/store/test_mcp_write_lock_dead_stamp.py` probes this surface.\n- Library facade: `rebar.append_session_log`, `create/comment/edit/transition` use the same command/append seams and shared write lock.\n- Automated callers: sync (`src/rebar/_store/sync.py:345`), inbound_translate, push, fsck/compact helpers all call `lock.write_lock`/`lock.acquire`, so the shared fix applies without per-caller patches.\n- Dual-direction diagnostics: `describe_lock_holder` now qualifies pid_state; doctor-locks and enrich-drain are string consumers, covered by `tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py` and `tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py`.\n- Reconciler `_ref_lock.py` / `_heartbeat.py`: N/A for this dead-pid-stamp gap. They use a git-ref lease with oid/fence progress and heartbeat renewal, not pid stamps or `os.kill` liveness.\n- Stamped-file locks (`enrich_drain`, compact trigger, snapshot GC): they share `stamped_file_is_stale` but have no fcntl leg, so immediate fcntl-authoritative reclaim is N/A; they retain the age ceiling and receive the diagnostic wording change.\n\nStructural guard decision: no new structural guard. The class has a single staleness authority (`_stamp_is_stale`) and the regression/unit/interface tests exercise both the true-positive and contrast paths; a static guard would either duplicate the function-level tests or overfit implementation text rather than a portable invariant.\n"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788240644275326001,"uuid":"605ba7fa-9e7d-42b1-aac5-774f2ee9e90a"}